# Raw Veo generations, before conform. Kept for RE-CUTTING, not for rendering.
#
# The conformed clips in ../clips are trimmed to exactly their allocation, so a
# cut can only ever move EARLIER against them. Snapping a cut to a pause in the
# narration also has to move cuts LATER, and the extra frames exist only here:
# every raw is 241 frames at 24fps (301 at 30) against a longest allocation of
# 279. Re-allocate, re-conform from these, re-render — no regeneration.
#
# Same storage deal as ../clips: ~970 MB of mp4 cannot go in git and the repo
# rejects anything over 10 MB, so what is committed is one pointer per shot and
# the bytes live as Lovable CDN assets.
#
# One wrinkle worth knowing: ep3_s01b's raw was lost from the sandbox and
# recovered from a re-generation probe (probe2_s01b.mp4). It was confirmed to be
# the same take by conforming it and measuring 46 dB PSNR against the shipped
# conformed s01b — re-encode noise, not different content.
*.mp4
